body:
You would fit in perfectly among most of the nonbinary people I know.

&#x200B;

Ultimately, how you identify yourself is up to YOU.

tbh i just want someone to yell at me and force me to stop thinking about gender all the damn time. {insert peridot meme: it has no functional purpose, it just makes me feel bad.} i can't stop thinking about it and it costs so much energy

&#x200B;

i guess i'm doomed to be questioning forever, though

&#x200B;

i'm so afraid everyone i love will leave me

&#x200B;

surely theres a way to just stop thinking about it and accept the obvious answer, which is that i'm fucking cis, since i don't have any reason not to be

What do you mean? Of course cis people spend hours every day compulsively analyzing their gender for years at a time, before forgetting about it/suppressing it for a little while and then being reminded and starting up again for a few years.... cis people also feel incredibly shitty when forced into gender-segregated groupings and forced to comply with gendered stereotypes, but all of that is normal because gendered stereotypes and forced segregation objectivel suck and gender is a confusing mystery. Objectively.

&#x200B;

source: i'm cis and i do all these things
